~ start
Hilda: *sniff sniff*
The large ogre looks at you as she sniffs the air. Her face cracks into a sly grin.
Hilda: Looks like we're having cat for dinner tonight!
She licks her lips and you suddenly feel that you can relate to how a can of tuna feels when you look at it.
- I'm here because Mio was worried about you! Don't eat me please.
    do WorldDialogueManager.MarkBossInteracted()
    Hilda: Mio huh? Very well. Let's play a game. If you lose you will be my dinner!
    do WorldDialogueManager.StartBossBattle()
    => END
- Ehm no! Actually I'm expired! I will see if I can go find you a fresh meal.
    do WorldDialogueManager.MarkBossInteracted()
    Hilda: Hmmph. Fine.
    do WorldDialogueManager.EndDialogue()
    => END
	
~ BackForMore
Hilda: Back again little morsel?
- Yes, but not as dinner! Let's play!
    do WorldDialogueManager.MarkBossInteracted()
    do WorldDialogueManager.StartBossBattle()
	 => END
- My name isn't morsel.
    do WorldDialogueManager.MarkBossInteracted()
	Hilda: Oh...
    do WorldDialogueManager.EndDialogue()
    => END
	
~ PostBattle
Hilda: Well guess I'll have to order takeaway tongiht.
She harrumphs but you can tell she is also happy you bested her.
You hear a click and a rumbling in the distance as if a path has opened.
Hilda: Here, have this! Hopefully it's useful to you.
"You received [color=yellow]Hilda[/color]'s card."
do WorldDialogueManager.EndDialogue()
=> END